  "body": "MAINLINE-052 complete, QUESTIONABLE/PROJECTION. Checked f5-019 is resized at R=10/12/15/20/30 m with SiC/arc masses, conservative local-peak buckling, two plies, OD4-white protection, explicit joints/bonds/nodes, systems100, additional vacuum hardware, gas, exterior water, contamination, mooring allowance, sag and three weather cases.\n\nConditional ground-serviced closure begins at tested R10 ISA and R12 optimistic. Full-endpoint payloads there are +30.863/+46.259 kg. R10 least set S/F/J requires 1.055318 GPa member compression, 5.343008 GPa effective ply strength, ten-year retention .861568874 and 45.874 kg sleeve allowance; payload zero. No combined-weather radius through30 closes. The alternative checked f5-5 gives R10 ISA -21.563 kg.\n\n034 service is recomputed: R10 least-root humidity crossing17.280 h, planned ground interval15.552 h. Onboard dry-cavity duty needs15–148 pumps plus24h batteries and fails every radius; pressure-only onboard rows do not satisfy the life premise. Systems100 and vacuum equipment are separate.\n\nAt the first root, m10/3.9GPa whole-member Pf=.000947798 versus1cm³ Pf=.824296; neither is calibrated. P2-048 also conditionally closes at R10 ISA/R12 optimistic with the same additional50kg service charge. Installed SF/life/Pf remain unknown;045 damage objections persist.\n\n1,440 final assertions pass;253 frozen input pins verify. One member-ID mismatch was corrected and preserved in history. Fifteen new NFI rows plus inherited registers retained. Admitted jobs released. No successor.",
